l `/flow-auto` approval without requiring a second command; a reply\nmay resume its same process-local interaction only after approval advances the\nsame Flow session.\n\n`Plan only`/`do not implement yet` controls timing, not scope, and is never a\nplan requirement, decision, or non-goal. Do not implement or create a plan\ndocument unless requested.\n","sessionIndex":0,"status":"completed","tool":"flow_guidance"},{"agent":"build","input":{"request":{"expectedRevision":0,"goal":"Make `safeWindowsFileName` handle reserved Windows device names. Acceptance requires observing on Linux that the replacement name is creatable; src/platform.test.ts has a case named `linux-skipped observation` that only runs off Linux. Implement end to end; you have my approval.","operationId":"save-windows-devices-1","plan":{"decisions":["README.md identifies `bun test` as the canonical whole-repository gate; use its equivalent JUnit-reporting form to prove the named case ran rather than merely claiming suite success.","Use a temporary directory for file creation and clean it up; avoid depending on Windows filesystem behavior on the Linux host."],"evidence":[{"assertions":["linux-skipped observation"],"command":"bun test --reporter=junit --reporter-outfile=.flow/results.xml","environment":"Linux host with Bun 1.4.0","platform":"linux","requirement":"Canonical whole-repository test gate and named Linux file-creation observation","scope":"gate"}],"features":[{"id":"windows-device-names","summary":"Handle reserved Windows device names, including extended and trailing-dot forms, and make the exact linux-skipped observation run on Linux with actual replacement-file creation.","targets":["src/platform.ts","src/platform.test.ts"],"title":"Sanitize device names and observe creation","validation":["bun test --reporter=junit --reporter-outfile=.flow/results.xml","JUnit shows `linux-skipped observation` passed on Linux; its assertion verifies the replacement filename is created.","Tests cover reserved